1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,450
12 perturbed Boltz-2 predictions: four systems, three runs each, every pocket broken on purpose.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,900
Shown only ipTM and pLDDT, an LLM agent called all 12 valid.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,050
Given the harness fact file, the same agent rejected all 12.

4
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,850
The facts: crystal contacts lost, buried polar atoms unpaired, a failed PoseBusters test.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,800
None of it shows in the confidence score.

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:27,950
PoseBusters: deep-learning docking often returns physically implausible poses, and RMSD does not catch it.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:33,550
On 557 Mac1 complexes, the best confidence score reached ROC AUC 0.76 for poses within 2 Å.

8
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,300
Runs N' Poses: co-folding methods largely memorise ligand poses.

9
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:42,500
The old way: CDK2 and ATP into Boltz-2. Back come a structure and ipTM 0.925.

10
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:47,000
The score stays high. Nothing flags the failure.

11
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,550
With the harness, the same input runs through 70 checks in six layers.

12
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:56,350
Each group names the tool that measures it: SIFTS, RDKit, PoseBusters, PLIP, OpenMM, spyrmsd.

13
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:59,500
Each check returns a value, a threshold and its origin.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,350
Same CDK2 input: verdict stop, each issue with its measured value.

15
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,200
Both stops are missing inputs: the Mg ion and a redocking control.

16
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:11,650
Boltz, Chai-1, Protenix, ColabFold, OpenFold3, DiffDock-L and Gnina run on Modal A100.

17
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:15,100
Vina runs on CPU. AlphaFold3, HADDOCK3 and pyDock outputs are checked.

18
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:20,469
New run. Target, ligand, tools and seeds are picked from the menus.

19
00:01:20,619 --> 00:01:25,337
Each pick is looked up live: UniProt, RCSB PDB, AlphaFold DB, PubChem, PDB CCD.

20
00:01:25,487 --> 00:01:36,211
Tools: Boltz-2, Chai-1, DiffDock-L and AutoDock Vina, five seeds each.

21
00:01:36,361 --> 00:01:40,450
Start run is not pressed. Next: a finished trypsin run with seven tools.

22
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:47,350
The finished run: request and 3PTB crystal beside the verdict, its issues and the Boltz-2 medoid.

23
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:51,750
Six tools ran on Modal A100, timed per seed. Vina ran on CPU.

24
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,950
The Ensemble lists each structure with pLDDT, confidence and PoseBusters.

25
00:01:55,745 --> 00:02:05,974
Every verdict carries its evidence: sources, files, thresholds and their origin.

26
00:02:06,768 --> 00:02:11,821
Agents call it through MCP and the HTTP API. Their steps appear in the Agent view.

27
00:02:12,321 --> 00:02:16,971
Run 3: balanced accuracy 0.50 vs 0.75 with the fact file, McNemar p 0.125.

28
00:02:17,121 --> 00:02:21,371
Over three runs: 12 of 12 perturbed Boltz-2 poses rejected, against 0 of 12.

29
00:02:21,521 --> 00:02:23,721
It also rejected valid DiffDock-L poses.

30
00:02:24,221 --> 00:02:31,221
Every run writes report.html, a provenance graph with sha256 checksums, PyMOL renders and figures.

